          ]
        },
        "metric": {
          "native_metric_wording": "$\\Phi_\\lambda(x)=\\inf_{u\\in\\mathbb{R}^d}\\{\\Phi(u)+\\|u-x\\|_2^2/(2\\lambda)\\}$, with $\\lambda=1/(2\\omega)$. Weak convexity makes the envelope differentiable, and $\\nabla\\Phi_\\lambda(x)=\\lambda^{-1}(x-\\operatorname{prox}_{\\lambda\\Phi}(x))$.",
          "formula_latex": "\\|\\nabla\\Phi_{1/(2\\omega)}(\\widehat{x})\\|_2^2",
          "threshold_latex": "\\varepsilon^2",
          "code": "moreau_envelope_stationarity",
          "description_paragraphs": [
            "$\\Phi_\\lambda(x)=\\inf_{u\\in\\mathbb{R}^d}\\{\\Phi(u)+\\|u-x\\|_2^2/(2\\lambda)\\}$, with $\\lambda=1/(2\\omega)$. Weak convexity makes the envelope differentiable, and $\\nabla\\Phi_\\lambda(x)=\\lambda^{-1}(x-\\operatorname{prox}_{\\lambda\\Phi}(x))$.",
            "The base loss is $\\ell(I,x)=\\|\\nabla\\Phi_\\lambda(x)\\|_2^2$ with tolerance $\\varepsilon^2$. The quantity $\\operatorname{prox}_{\\lambda\\Phi}$ defines only the performance metric and adds no information interface."
